assistant: Subject: Send an Idempotency-Key header when creating orders

Vendor 2026-10-01 seems to stop saving orders that are sent without the `Idempotency-Key` header. The published spec marks that header optional but recommended. The POST still returns 200 with an order id, but `GET /orders/{id}` then returns 404, so `create_order` hands agents an id they can't read back. This cause is my best inference, not something I confirmed: the two recordings are the same except for the vendor version (and a `created_at` format change that doesn't affect lookup), and this header is the only documented request option. `create_order` now sends a new `idempotency-key` (from `randomUUID()`) on each call. That's correct here because each call is a separate order attempt. The output is unchanged, and it only adds a request header the spec already allows, so the 2026-01-01 version should behave the same. `pnpm typecheck` and `pnpm lint` pass, and all tests pass except two: the repro test and the v1 `order-create.json` fixture fail with UNMATCHED_REQUEST because their recordings don't include the new header. That is the expected result. Re-recording both with fiks will confirm the fix against the live vendor.

